<title>BELGIUM: Italy did not exert pressure on EMU forecasts--EU.</title>
<headline>Italy did not exert pressure on EMU forecasts--EU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy did not exert political pressure to obtain a more favourable result in the European Union's economic outlook for the country, EU commissioner Yves Thibault de Silguy said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;May I say that anybody, any government, can cry, moan, roll on the ground,&quot; de Silguy said at a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;It seems to me the duty of the Commission is to maintain and safeguard the credibility of the Commission. Had there been any pressure it would have been pointless.&quot;</p>
<p>Italy's 1997 budget deficit was forecast at 3.2 percent of Gross Domestic Product, slightly above the Maastricht treaty's target.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6838</p>
</text>
